{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"agent_message","text":"The test now forms a three-voter cluster with one nonvoter, partitions it into `a,n` and `b,c`, and waits for `b,c` to elect a higher-term leader and apply a new command.\n\nIt also waits until both of `a`’s serial send paths to each voter have made a post-partition attempt. With pipelining disabled through the supported transport interface, that accounts for old voter replies before verification begins. The result will distinguish a completed error, a successful verification, and an observation timeout.\n"}}
